Modifications by lightmux (all marked with a `[lightmux]` comment):

  terminal-emulator/
    - Removed JNI.java and src/main/jni/ (the local PTY C code). lightmux
      attaches to remote hosts and never forks a local process.
    - Added TerminalTransport.java: an interface abstracting the byte channel
      (start / write / updateSize / close) so the emulator core is transport
      agnostic.
    - Rewrote TerminalSession.java to drive a TerminalTransport instead of a
      forkpty()'d process: removed shell path/cwd/args/env, waitpid, SIGKILL
      and /proc-based cwd lookup; added reconnect(TerminalTransport) which
      swaps the transport while preserving the emulator and its scrollback.
    - TerminalSession.java: reconnect() also replaces both IO queues with fresh
      ByteQueue instances instead of reusing the ones cleanupResources() closed
      (upstream queues are single-use, since a dead process ends the session for
      good). Each transport generation captures its own queues, so threads left
      over from the previous connection stay bound to the old, already-closed
      queues and terminate on their own.
    - TerminalSession.java: the transport-closed message now carries its
      generation, and the main-thread handler re-checks it before tearing the
      session down, so a close notification from a superseded transport cannot
      shut down the connection that replaced it.
    - All other files, including ByteQueue.java, are unmodified from upstream.

  terminal-view/
    - Unmodified from upstream.

Upstream unit tests under terminal-emulator/src/test/ are kept verbatim and run
in CI, so any accidental regression in the vendored emulator core is caught.

